y have severe  repercussions for ongoing litigation  because the president's defenders argued  that the Democrats should have waited  for the courts to decide a lot of these  evidentiary issues and procured more  evidence in the house before going to  the trial in the Senate the thing is  there's active ongoing litigation over  the subpoena to former White House  Counsel dawn McGann the White House has  argued that the courts have no business  adjudicating the White House's refusal  to turn over dawn McGann for testimony  the DOJ as recently as last month argued  that courts can't adjudicate the  privileges used for separation of powers  issues the thing is on the floor of the  Senate the president's attorney Jay  Sekulow argued that Democrats rushed  things and should have waited for the  judiciary to weigh in the rush to  impeachment to not wait for a decision  from a court on an issue is important as  executive privilege  the president's opponents in their rush  to impeach have refused to wait for  complete judicial review other lawyers  for the president are in court saying  the exact opposite of what they're  telling you today they're saying you  cannot enforce congressional subpoenas  that's non judicial that is such a  stunning admission and contradiction  that if I was one of the lawyers working  on that particular case the Don Magan  case I would probably file an emergency  motion with the court of appeals saying  that the Trump administration is  basically conceded the issue and at the  court of appeal needs to compel the  testimony of Don began now there's sort  of a pet theory going around the  internet that Chief Justice Roberts as  the presiding judge over this trial can  save a lot of these issues and can rise  up and can prevent some of the  obfuscation from the Republicans I would  say that that theory was dealt a serious  blow during the first day of the trial  when Roberts really didn't do anything  and wasn't even given some of the power  that the Democrats want him to receive  and that Roberts is really just going to  try to disappear and fade into the  background like his predecessor William  Rehnquist did really the only thing that  Chief Justice Roberts did on the first  day when he chose to speak was to dress  down both sides and say that neither is  upholding the decorum that is required  for these proceedings I think it is  appropriate at this point for me  to admonish both the house managers and  the President's Council in equal terms  to remember that they are addressing the  world's greatest deliberative body one  reason it has earned that title is  because its members avoid speaking in a  manner and using language that is not  conducive to civil discourse but that's  sort of par for the course that's what  you would expect the Chief Justice to do  to fade into the background and let the  political bodies deal with the political  questions so I would expect more of the  same more fading into the background and  both sides in all the issues of course  in one of the biggest surprises senator  Ted Cruz apparently singled me out by  intentionally misusing the famous table  pounding quote you know there's an old  saying that if you have the facts you  bang the facts if you have the law you  bang the law if you don't have either  you bang the table now of course I can't  be certain that senator Cruz is singling  me out by misusing a quote that I've  used many times on this particular  channel but he really does feel like  he's turning it on its head when the  Democrats whether you liked it or not  spent hours upon hours talking about all  the evidence that the White House is  holding back the fact that they haven't  produced a single document or allowed  any White House witnesses to testify in  the House or the Senate  whether you liked it or not they were  talking about the substance of our  gyun's and making use of the evidence  and law that is relevant to this  particular case and of course the  craziest thing of all is that wow this  is all going on in the u.s. President  Trump is in Davos where he gave a press  conference where he specifically bragged  about how he is not giving the Democrats  any evidence and that he's holding it  all back we're doing very well I got to  watch enough I thought our team did a  very good job but honestly we have all  the material they don't have the  material now if I was trying to be  charitable here I would say that  President Trump is just saying that all  of the evidence is in his favor but he  specifically uses the word material  referring to the actual physical things  themselves and not their metaphorical  significance we have all the material  they don't have them at  so it really does seem like the  president is bragging about obstructing  Congress and preventing them from  getting any of the relevant evidence and  not the fact that he's just bragging  about how the evidence supports himself  it really is sort of hilarious that the  president always seems to say the quiet  part out loud and by hilarious I mean  that in the saddest way possible so the  Democratic argument often boils down to  saying that the president is a liar liar  and his pants are on fire and if his  pants really are on fire then he should  really buy some new ones so mr.  president if you're looking for a custom  slim cut suit that is shockingly  affordable I can't recommend endo Chino  highly enough all of my suits are now  made by Indochina including this brown  checked three-piece and if this suit  looks familiar it's because I  unapologetically stole the design from  Blake Scott like just know that  imitation is the highest form of  flattery there's just one thing I wanted  to change though I wanted to change the  lapel from a notch to a peak and with  Indo Chino not only could I choose the  fabric so it was exactly the same but I  could tweak it so that it was a hundred  percent my own and a hundred percent  custom which is exactly what I did